{"id": "EUVD-2026-59301", "enisaUuid": "9332f449-7e06-3032-bca2-a2db49900920", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mask pseudo pointer values in verifier logs\n\nprint_bpf_insn() masks ldimm64 immediates for pointer-bearing pseudo\nsources when pointer leaks are not allowed, but the mask only covers\nBPF_PSEUDO_MAP_FD and BPF_PSEUDO_MAP_VALUE.\n\nBPF_PSEUDO_MAP_IDX, BPF_PSEUDO_MAP_IDX_VALUE, and BPF_PSEUDO_BTF_ID can\nalso be resolved to kernel pointer values before the verifier log prints\nthe instruction. Include them in the existing pointer classification so\nthe log prints 0x0 instead of the rewritten address.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:55:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b767a5d7c6cb595f9feb00b5af96191a59efca26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6181239115e19cda4b483a2604193a9379cbd28f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c727b3d50ecb0f4992a964360771040a84026914", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b96cb1235fcaa687291b1e1d910f0930d1939919", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c53d16b174dd9e02243fc0e85089e2aa6a0d21a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72a85e9464a5332fb2cd7efd26d9295275ceda2d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-759v-33rj-5hjh", "CVE-2026-72402"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "072e44f9-674f-333c-9942-8aae078f6f4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "1e31e4d8-d10a-3065-add6-9b2843f1e3d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "32e40049-9d75-3cad-95a4-e6f459272465", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4976b718c3551faba2c0616ef55ebeb74db1c5ca <6181239115e19cda4b483a2604193a9379cbd28f"}, {"id": "4457a4b4-1965-3a16-b47d-4faaec07d3a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "4